## Course Overview

This course covers the dynamic modeling, analysis, and feedback control system design principles for industrial processes. Students gain practical insights into controller tuning and stability criteria for single-input single-output (SISO) control loops.

## Topics Covered

- Process Dynamics & Transfer Function Derivation
- First-Order and Second-Order System Responses
- PID Controller Design and Tuning Methods (Ziegler-Nichols, Cohen-Coon)
- Closed-Loop Stability Analysis (Routh-Hurwitz, Nyquist Criteria)
- Advanced Control Architectures (Feedforward, Cascade, Ratio Control)

